course: dictionary
lesson: 681
title: Ballot
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A ballot is a secret way of voting. You write your choice on a paper, or use a machine, and nobody can see what you chose. The paper you vote on is also called a ballot paper.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «In a secret ballot nobody can see how a person voted.» The word secret tells you the vote is hidden, so ballot here means a secret vote.
explain: Ballot can also mean a random draw in the UK and Australia, where tickets or school places are given out by chance. It can be a verb too: to ballot people means to ask them to vote. Check the sentence to see which meaning fits.
fact: A ballot is a secret way of voting, by writing on paper or using a machine.
fact: «Ballot» can also mean the paper you vote on, called a ballot paper.
fact: In the UK and Australia, a ballot can be a random draw to decide who gets tickets or school places.
fact: «Secret ballot» means nobody can see how you voted.
fact: A ballot box is the box where voting papers are put.
exercise: «In a secret ballot nobody can see how a person voted.» What does secret ballot mean? | *A vote where nobody can see your choice | A vote shouted out loud in class | A vote held only on Fridays | A vote where everyone can see each choice
exercise: In a school council election, you put your choice on a paper and drop it in the box. What is the paper called? | A show of hands | A seat plan | *A ballot paper | A lolly
exercise: In Australia, school places are decided by «ballot», a random draw. What does ballot mean here? | A kind of sports game | A way of shouting votes out loud | *A random draw to decide who gets something | A list of school rules
test: «Fair voting needs a secret ballot, so nobody votes just to please a best friend.» Why is a secret ballot fair? | It is quicker to count | You get a lolly for voting | Everyone must shout their vote out loud | *Nobody can see your choice, so you vote as you really think
test: Ms Lee says, "We will ballot the class on the trip." What does ballot mean here? | *To ask people to vote | To count the lollies | To lose a game | To write a letter home
exam: Why are no lollies given for votes? | Because lollies are too expensive to share | Because a secret ballot is only for adults | Because voting is always done loudly | *Because a lolly for a vote is a bribe
